# agent-example — copy to `.env` and uncomment what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so keep real keys out of it. The
# `dev` and `start` scripts load `.env` with node's `--env-file-if-exists`,
# so a missing file is fine — everything below is OPTIONAL, and with nothing
# set the example runs our own engine on the scripted `mockModel`.

# Everything below chooses what the New-session FORM STARTS ON, and what the
# first session opens with. After that the page decides — pick an agent, a
# model and a mode in the sidebar, and open as many sessions as you want.
#
# ── Agent ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which agent the form starts on:
#   mock             the scripted agent from @sigx/ai-agent/testing
#   sigx             our engine (modelAgent) — see "Model" below
#   claude-code      Claude Code, through @sigx/ai-agent-claude-code
#   codex-cli        Codex CLI, through @sigx/ai-agent-codex-cli (`codex app-server`)
#   copilot-cli      GitHub Copilot CLI, through @sigx/ai-agent-copilot-cli (the SDK's bundled runtime)
#   acp:gemini       Gemini CLI, through @sigx/ai-agent-acp
#   acp:cursor       the Cursor CLI agent, through @sigx/ai-agent-acp
#   acp:claude-code  Claude Code via its ACP bridge (claude-agent-acp)
#   acp:codex-cli    Codex via its ACP bridge (codex-acp)
#   acp:copilot-cli  GitHub Copilot CLI's own ACP server (copilot --acp)
# Every harness runs on your own login / key. Unset = sigx. A harness that
# cannot start says why IN THE FORM — an explicit choice never silently
# becomes a different agent — and is offered greyed out with the reason on it:
# a missing CLI gets an install hint, anything else (not signed in, an SDK
# error) the error message. (The SIGX_ prefix is not decoration: a bare
# AI_AGENT is already set by some of the tooling you may be running this
# from, Claude Code included.)
#SIGX_AI_AGENT=claude-code

# The directory a harness works in (its session cwd) — the form's default,
# editable per session. Unset = the directory the server was started from.
# Ignored by sigx and mock.
#SIGX_AI_CWD=C:/work/my-repo

# A specific executable for the chosen harness instead of the PATH lookup —
# a locally built CLI, a shim outside PATH. For claude-code this is the
# adapter's pathToClaudeCodeExecutable (the SDK bundles its own binary
# otherwise). Unset = the harness's default command on PATH.
#SIGX_AI_AGENT_COMMAND=C:/tools/codex/codex.cmd

# ── Model (SIGX_AI_AGENT=sigx only) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The form's default model. With a key set, sigx offers several and the pane's
# Settings panel switches a RUNNING session between them.
# 'anthropic' | 'openai' | 'mock'. Unset = inferred: anthropic if
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, else openai if OPENAI_API_KEY is set, else mock.
#SIGX_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Model id for the chosen provider. Unset = that provider's default:
# claude-opus-5 (anthropic) / gpt-5 (openai).
#SIGX_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ── Keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The VALUE is read only by the official SDKs — but the PRESENCE of a key is
# what picks the provider when SIGX_AI_PROVIDER is unset (agent.server.ts, and
# the banner dev-server.mjs prints). Neither reaches the browser: vite.config.ts
# swaps agent.server.ts for a stub in the client build.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# A harness child process gets an ALLOWLISTED environment (PATH, HOME, proxy
# vars, …) plus the vendor variables its adapter passes through — nothing
# else from this file reaches it:
#   claude-code       ANTHROPIC_*, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR   (or just the CLI's own login)
#   codex-cli         OPENAI_API_KEY, CODEX_HOME        (or `codex login`)
#   copilot-cli       COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, COPILOT_HOME   (or `copilot login`)
#   acp:gemini        GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY
#   acp:cursor        CURSOR_API_KEY, CURSOR_AUTH_TOKEN
#   acp:claude-code   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
#   acp:codex-cli     OPENAI_API_KEY, CODEX_HOME
#   acp:copilot-cli   COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, COPILOT_HOME
#GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#CURSOR_API_KEY=...

# ── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port for both dev-server.mjs and server.mjs. Unset = 5320.
#PORT=5320
